                <pb facs="0199" n="1033" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1033"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/9586</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Sharp</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-27T23:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 27, 1918, 11 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 28, 7.27 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4604. War Trade Board [from McFadden]:</p>
                <p>No. 300. Referring our No. 284 of July 20. For your information. The British
                    delegate on I. B. C., Paris, has received from his Government a telegram
                    requesting Japan’s participation in preparation of the black list pending
                    further communication from London. Arguments used at the meeting yesterday
                    against such participation in Paris were: First, if Japan were asked, it might
                    necessitate inviting representatives of other Associated Governments not now
                    represented, with the result of increasing size committee, complicating
                    discussions, and retarding decisions; second, Paris committee is not concerned
                    with question relative to Far East which your committee handles. McFadden.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sharp</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
